cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ADAMAS: Cryptographically Binding a Diamond's Physical Signature to Its On-Chain Provenance"
authors:
  - family-names: Kandukoori
    given-names: Aarush
    email: akandukoori@andrew.cmu.edu
    affiliation: "School of Computer Science, Carnegie Mellon University"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-21"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aarushkandukoori/adamas-diamond-provenance"
abstract: >-
  Distributed ledgers give diamond provenance systems tamper-evident records
  but do not bind those records to physical stones. ADAMAS derives a
  cryptographic key from a stone's crystallographic defect structure so that
  possession of the physical stone is a prerequisite for every provenance
  operation. This repository packages the paper, simulation harness, and
  bit-exact verification artifacts.
keywords:
  - diamond provenance
  - fuzzy vault
  - cryptographic binding
  - reproducibility
